From: lonerOrz <lonerOrz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gud: clamp TV mode count to the buffer capacity

gud_connector_add_tv_mode() derives num_modes from the USB transfer length,
which clang cannot prove is bounded by buf_len. Its ThinLTO unroller can thus
emit an out-of-bounds iteration, and FORTIFY_SOURCE's memchr() check fails the
link with "__read_overflow: detected read beyond size of object".

Clamp num_modes to the number of modes the buffer can actually hold.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
@@ -395,7 +395,7 @@
 		goto free;
 	}

-	num_modes = ret / GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN;
+	num_modes = min(ret / GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN, GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM);
 	for (i = 0; i < num_modes; i++) {
 		char *mode = &buf[i * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN];

